 "observations": [
  "The page number «219» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 104», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature «28*» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The page has no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 97r, O 152v,» and «N 63v.», the letters raised (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-218 (JP2 0238-0250): «Viginti1) gradus Librae» (L03), «Viginti quinque2) gradus Librae» (L15) and «Triginta3) gradus Librae» (L23), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Libra, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold. The heads of the columns of the first field as on p. 218 (JP2 0250, L04-L07), from Libra to Pisces, with «Horoscopus» in each and without notes (L05-L08). The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields. Note i is set «i-i)», the two raised letters joined by a hyphen, with one parenthesis, and its lemma «10-55» joins the first and the last number of the minutes of Aquarius in the second field (L17-L22) by a hyphen; the paired notes of p. 218 (JP2 0250) are set «c)—c)».",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-218 (JP2 0238-0250), are a third, a half and two thirds of one number. In the second and the third field it is the last number of the field: 201° 5′ (L22) gives 67° 1.7′, 100° 32.5′ and 134° 3.3′, printed 67° 2′, 100° 32′ and 134° 3′ (L16); 200° 39′ (L30) gives 66° 53′, 100° 19.5′ and 133° 46′, printed 66° 53′, 100° 20′ and 133° 46′ (L24). In the first field 67° 30′, 101° 15′ and 135° 0′ (L04) are a third, a half and two thirds of 202° 30′, 20′ less than the last number of the field, 202° 50′ (L14), whose thirds are 67° 36.7′, 101° 25′ and 135° 13.3′.",
  "The columns, as on p. 218 (JP2 0250): in Libra the three fields lie below the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Libra for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′; 6° 10′, 12° 21′, 18° 33′, 24° 45′, 30° 59′, 37° 14′), by 11′ to 59′, 23′ to 1° 34′ and 26′ to 1° 41′; at the end of Sagittarius by 3° 4′, 2° 24′ and 1° 46′ (107° 15′, 107° 55′ and 108° 33′ for 110° 19′). The columns pass the oblique ascensions between 25° of Capricornus and 5° of Aquarius and end 22° 50′, 21° 5′ and 20° 39′ above them (202° 50′, 201° 5′ and 200° 39′ for 180°). From 10° of Capricornus to the end of Pisces the second field lies 24′ to 52′ below the mean of the first and the third, and 1° 5′ at 15° of Aquarius (note p).",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the rule of the heads, by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 20° of Libra in the first field (note a, L12: C's 24 against O's 23, the steps 6° 8′ and 5° 54′ against 5° 8′ and 6° 54′), at 5° of Scorpius and of Sagittarius in the first (notes b and e, L09: O's 42 against C's 32; the 79 of O and N against C's 77, the steps 5° 56′ and 5° 42′ against 3° 56′ and 7° 42′), at 25° and 30° of Scorpius in the first (notes c and d, L13-L14: C's 41 and 47 against O's 61 and 67, which are no numbers of minutes), at 10° of Capricornus in the first (note f, L10: C's 54 against O's 34, the steps 5° 19′ and 5° 16′ against 4° 59′ and 5° 36′), at 30° of Aquarius in the second (note h, L22: the 168 of O and N against C's 169, the steps 4° 50′ and 5° 20′ against 5° 50′ and 4° 20′), in the quadrature and the trine of the third (notes k and l, L24: O's 100° 20′ and 133° 46′, a half and two thirds of 200° 39′, against C's 100° 32′ and 134° 3′, the quadrature and the trine of the second field, L16), at 30° of Scorpius and 25° and 30° of Sagittarius in the third (notes m, n and o, L30, L29: C's 73, 1 and 33 against O's 72, 30 and 3; with C's 73 the steps into Sagittarius are 6° 17′ and 6° 5′, with O's 72 5° 17′ and 7° 5′, and with C's 1 and 33 the steps of Sagittarius fall evenly, 5° 53′, 5° 45′, 5° 32′ and 5° 13′ into Capricornus). In the minutes of Aquarius in the second field (note i, L17-L22) C's 27, 40, 45, 45, 55, 45 are, but for the fifth, the minutes of the first field (L09-L14: 27, 40, 45, 45, 45, 45; «cfr. supra»).",
  "At 15° of Aquarius in the third field (note p, L27) the 1 of O and N is the nearer: 155° 1′ gives the steps 5° 2′ and 4° 50′, between 5° 3′ and 4° 45′, and lies 16′ above the first field (154° 45′), as the third field does at 5° and 10° of Aquarius (29′ and 19′), where C's 155° 50′, which the edition adopts, gives 5° 51′ and 4° 1′. At 10° of Pisces in the third field (note r, L26) O's 49 is the nearer: it gives the steps 5° 15′ and 5° 20′, C's 39, which the edition adopts, 5° 5′ and 5° 30′, the other steps of the column being 5° 9′ to 5° 18′. At 25° of Capricornus in the first field (note g, L13) C's 35 gives the steps 5° 0′ and 4° 40′, O's 55 5° 20′ and 4° 20′; at 30° of Aquarius and 20° of Pisces in the third (notes q and s, L30, L28) the readings differ by 3′ and 2′; none of these is decided.",
  "Without variants: in the first field 107° 15′ at 30° of Sagittarius (L14) lies 1° 0′ and 40′ below the neighbouring fields, 108° 15′ (p. 218, JP2 0250, L29) and 107° 55′ (L22), between the steps 4° 35′ and 6° 20′; with 108° 15′ they would be 5° 35′ and 5° 20′.",
  "A point after the 23 at 20° of Libra in the second field (L20) and a speck on the rule before the 10 of Aquarius in L17 are specks; not transcribed. Italics: «om.», «cfr. supra»."
 ],
